Code-level safety net (rationale for accepting deferral of #5 / #6)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Three reinforcing layers prevent silent reintroduction of the bug:

1. Wire-format pin (backend):
   `TestPayload_NoIconField` walks `webpush.Payload`'s reflected
   struct fields and rejects any field whose name OR JSON tag starts
   with the literal string "icon" (case-insensitive). A future PR that
   re-adds `Icon string `json:"icon,omitempty"` will fail this test
   immediately.

2. Wire-shape pin (backend):
   `TestPayload_JSONShape_OmitsIcon` marshals a fully-populated
   Payload to JSON and asserts the resulting bytes do not contain the
   substring `"icon"`. This catches the case where a future Payload
   embeds a sub-struct that itself transmits an icon field.

3. Renderer pin (service worker):
   `web/src/sw/__tests__/sw.test.ts` synthesises a real `push` event,
   dispatches it through the SW's registered handler, captures the
   `self.registration.showNotification(title, options)` call, and
   asserts `options.icon === undefined` for three scenarios:
     - typical alert payload (no icon on the wire);
     - critical alert payload (also asserts requireInteraction=true);
     - rogue payload that includes a stray `icon` key — the SW's
       typed PushPayload omits the field, so it cannot leak through
       even if a future backend regression starts emitting it.

Slice 0010 closes the user-reported "duplicate icon" bug at the
contract level. A human reviewer with an Android device should still
visually confirm criterion #5 once before final merge; the DEFERRED
mark is a reminder of that, not a blocker.

